rockchip: usb: report rockusb as loader; honor K_FW_RESET reboot subcodes

Rockchip host tools (rkdeveloptool / upgrade_tool / RKDevTool) classify a
device purely by bcdUSB & 1: 0x0200 = maskrom (BootROM), 0x0201 = loader.
Mainline g_dnl keeps the default 0x0200, so rockusb shows up as Maskrom and
tools enable maskrom-only paths (0x471/0x472 control transfers) that this
gadget cannot serve. Vendor U-Boot sets 0x0201 in its g_dnl_bind_fixup.

Also implement the rkusb_set_reboot_flag() weak hook: tools send K_FW_RESET
with subcode 0x03 (reboot to BootROM download / maskrom) or 0x06 (reboot to
loader). Writing the matching flag to the boot mode register lets
'upgrade_tool uf' and 'rkdeveloptool rd 3' bounce the board from our rockusb
into real maskrom, mirroring stock loader behavior.

Upstream-Status: Pending (against v2026.07)
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c	2026-08-17 19:57:20.112408388 +0000
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c	2026-08-17 19:57:41.943812044 +0000
@@ -226,8 +226,35 @@
 	else
 		put_unaligned(CONFIG_USB_GADGET_PRODUCT_NUM, &dev->idProduct);
 
+	/*
+	 * Rockchip host tools read bcdUSB & 1 as loader-vs-maskrom. Without
+	 * the odd value they treat rockusb as a BootROM device and speak the
+	 * 0x471/0x472 maskrom protocol this gadget does not implement.
+	 */
+	if (!strcmp(name, "usb_dnl_rockusb"))
+		put_unaligned(cpu_to_le16(0x0201), &dev->bcdUSB);
+
 	return 0;
 }
+
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_ROCKUSB)
+void rkusb_set_reboot_flag(int flag);
+void rkusb_set_reboot_flag(int flag)
+{
+	/*
+	 * K_FW_RESET subcodes sent by Rockchip host tools ("uf" bounces a
+	 * loader-mode device back to real maskrom this way):
+	 * 0x03 = reboot to BootROM download, 0x06 = reboot to loader.
+	 */
+	if (!CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG)
+		return;
+
+	if (flag == 0x03)
+		writel(BOOT_BROM_DOWNLOAD, CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG);
+	else if (flag == 0x06)
+		writel(BOOT_LOADER, CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG);
+}
+#endif /* CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_ROCKUSB */
 #endif /* CONFIG_USB_GADGET_DOWNLOAD */
 
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USB_GADGET_DWC2_OTG) && !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DM_USB_GADGET)
